{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of pairs enumerating the sequence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example enumerates the characters of the string “Swift” and prints","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each character along with its place in the string.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["for (n, c) in \"Swift\".enumerated() {","    print(\"\\(n): '\\(c)'\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"0: 'S'\"","\/\/ Prints \"1: 'w'\"","\/\/ Prints \"2: 'i'\"","\/\/ Prints \"3: 'f'\"","\/\/ Prints \"4: 't'\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you enumerate a collection, the integer part of each pair is a counter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the enumeration, but is not necessarily the index of the paired value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These counters can be used as indices only in instances of zero-based,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer-indexed collections, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContiguousArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other collections the counters may be out of range or of the wrong type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to use as an index. To iterate over the elements of a collection with its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices, use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"zip(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example iterates over the indices and elements of a set, building a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list consisting of indices of names with five or fewer letters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let names: Set = [\"Sofia\", \"Camilla\", \"Martina\", \"Mateo\", \"Nicolás\"]","var shorterIndices: [Set<String>.Index] = []","for (i, name) in zip(names.indices, names) {","    if name.count <= 5 {","        shorterIndices.append(i)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now that the ","type":"text"},{"code":"shorterIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array holds the indices of the shorter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"names","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, you can use those indices to access elements in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["for i in shorterIndices {","    print(names[i])","}","\/\/ Prints \"Sofia\"","\/\/ Prints \"Mateo\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(1)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a sequence of pairs ("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" represents a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"consecutive integer starting at zero and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" represents an element of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS"},{"introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iPadOS"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"10.10","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"macOS"},{"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"visionOS"},{"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"2.0","beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"enumerated()","externalID":"s:STsE10enumerateds18EnumeratedSequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:s23LazyPrefixWhileSequenceV8IteratorV","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enumerated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","text":"EnumeratedSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"symbolKind":"method"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/LazyPrefixWhileSequence\/Iterator\/enumerated()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/LazyPrefixWhileSequence","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/LazyPrefixWhileSequence\/Iterator"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"pat